 "equipment_type": "Make-up air unit controls (heating and ventilating unit)",
 "applies_to": "AbsolutAire heating and ventilating units with the UC-3 Lite control system.",
 "summary": "The UC-3 Lite is AbsolutAire's simpler heat-and-vent unit controller, running the burner to a space or discharge temperature with optional VFD and mixed-air damper. It joins a BACnet MS/TP network with its MAC address set on DIP switches. The BMS turns the unit off, on or to auto with network_UnitEnableCommand, sets occupancy, mode and heat setpoints, and can send its own space temperature.",
 "bacnet_transport": [
  "BACnet MS/TP"
 ],
 "firmware": null,
 "default_device_instance": "3640 followed by the MAC address (MAC 25 = 364025)",
 "access_inferred": false,
 "notes": [
  "The Network Points List in the guide is printed as an image; values were keyed by hand from the rendered page and checked row by row.",
  "The table also lists the controller's physical I/O as 'Hardware Input n' / 'Hardware Output n' (14 rows) without a BACnet object type; they are left out. The guide marks them do-not-write.",
  "For many binary objects the guide prints only the facet text, e.g. Boolean (ALARM;NORMAL), without saying which state is 1; the occupancy, HVAC mode and control-type commands give 0/1 meanings.",
  "MV 11 network_UnitEnableCommand is OFF / ON / AUTO; the guide does not print the state numbers. AUTO lets the unit cycle per BV 14 and BV 15.",
  "Objects marked [DO NOT WRITE] or factory configuration are listed as read-only."
 ],
